WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.310
- So this week, I've
been sharing wise words

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.890
from authors who inspire me.

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:04.999
Listen to this quote,

00:00:04.999 --> 00:00:07.607
"Even the worst thing
that can happen to you

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:11.730
"is meant to happen because
it's going to push you to grow."

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.263
It's by Don Miguel Ruiz,

00:00:13.263 --> 00:00:16.012
the author of the prolific
book, "The Four Agreements",

00:00:16.012 --> 00:00:18.750
that's from his newer book,
"The Fifth Agreement".

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:19.583
I'm not the only one

00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:21.480
who finds those words
inspirational though,

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.891
Kailyn in our house seat says

00:00:22.891 --> 00:00:25.274
it's propelled her to rethink things.

00:00:25.274 --> 00:00:28.200
So Kailyn, you had a
pretty rough 2020, right?

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.033
- Yeah.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.837
Hi, Kelly, it's so nice to meet you.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.050
Yeah, 2020 was rough.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:39.050
With everything with the
elections and with the pandemic.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.637
I'm a neonatal intensive care nurse

00:00:41.637 --> 00:00:46.040
and so I've seen first
hand moms being separated

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.970
from their babies.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:52.970
And so that was tough and
is still tough for me,

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.380
as a mom myself.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:59.513
I have two grown, beautiful daughters

00:00:59.513 --> 00:01:01.833
who my husband and I adopted.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.410
My husband and I are white
and our daughters are Black,

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:09.230
and this summer past at the height

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:13.340
of the Black Lives Matter Movement,

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.990
my brother posted something on Facebook

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.122
that really upset me.

00:01:19.122 --> 00:01:21.233
- Oh my gosh, I'm sorry.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.320
You know what, I'm gonna
be honest with you,

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.580
that has happened with a lot of families,

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.583
especially in 2020.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.610
Be it politics, religion,
every day issues,

00:01:34.772 --> 00:01:37.060
I think there's been
a lot of communicating

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:40.085
and some of it's super
negative and hardcore

00:01:40.085 --> 00:01:42.400
and it's even harder
when it's your family.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.860
And you love them so much

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.960
and you're like, look, we
disagree on this major thing

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.140
and I'd like to be able
to talk to you about it,

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.207
in a healthy kind of way.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:56.040
Why does that quote really helps you?

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.010
Is it because you're kind of looking at it

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.257
as a struggle, but it's worth it?

00:02:00.257 --> 00:02:02.960
Because in the end, there's
gotta be a reason, right?

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:03.793
- Right.

00:02:03.793 --> 00:02:06.443
So when he posted what he did,

00:02:06.443 --> 00:02:09.397
as a mother of Black daughters,

00:02:09.397 --> 00:02:13.652
I felt that I needed to stick
up for them and say something

00:02:13.652 --> 00:02:16.500
and I felt that he didn't understand

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.234
the depth of the meaning behind

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:22.472
what the Black Lives
Matter Movement was about.

00:02:22.472 --> 00:02:27.090
And so I commented, and
other family members

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.880
jumped on and commented,
his friends commented,

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.380
and it turned into this big ordeal.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.670
My feelings were hurt,

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:40.450
because I felt like he
wasn't understanding

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.328
and respecting my daughters' experiences.

00:02:43.328 --> 00:02:45.470
And his feelings were hurt

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:48.283
because it all took
place in a public forum,

00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:50.907
and he told me to lose his contacts,

00:02:50.907 --> 00:02:55.907
and family is important
to me, and it hurt.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.283
- Wow.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:02:59.973
I mean...

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.970
I don't know...

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.841
That's a tricky thing to talk about.

00:03:06.841 --> 00:03:11.841
You know, because I feel like on one hand,

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.935
it's like, okay, well thank
you for showing me who you are,

00:03:14.935 --> 00:03:17.231
and protecting your babies,

00:03:17.231 --> 00:03:19.493
you know, but on the
other hand, you're like,

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.370
if we can't do this as a family,

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.660
if we can't find some
kind of common ground,

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.700
if we can't see from
each other's perspective

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.150
and we're family,

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:31.137
how in the world is the rest
of the world gonna make it?

00:03:31.137 --> 00:03:32.350
You know?

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:36.205
I'm really sorry, that's a hard situation.

00:03:36.205 --> 00:03:39.061
But I'm very glad that Don Miguel Ruiz

00:03:39.061 --> 00:03:40.321
is joining us later,

00:03:40.321 --> 00:03:42.570
because he's got some wisdom to impart

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.860
and not only, hopefully for you Kailyn,

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.860
but also just for everybody else,

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.960
how to make 2021 our best year yet.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.740
I'm sure you're not the only family...

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:54.050
I'm 100% sure you are not the only family

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.220
to experience devastation like that

00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:00.170
in such an emotional way
between your family roots.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:03.249
So here we are, day six of 2021

00:04:03.249 --> 00:04:07.271
and if you haven't fully
scrubbed off the dirt from 2020,

00:04:07.271 --> 00:04:10.410
it's okay 'cause we are
helping you get there all week

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.640
with our series, Well,
That Sucked, Moving On.

00:04:14.994 --> 00:04:18.106
♪ Well that sucked, moving on ♪

00:04:18.106 --> 00:04:19.960
- That's my favorite inflection,

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.353
well, that sucked.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:23.850
More than 20 years ago,

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:27.310
my next guest published one of
the most popular modern books

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:28.837
on spiritual enlightenment.

00:04:28.837 --> 00:04:31.470
"The Four Agreements" is
all about finding happiness

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.048
within yourself through integrity

00:04:33.048 --> 00:04:34.708
and not taking anything personally,

00:04:34.708 --> 00:04:36.390
not making any assumptions,

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.510
and by simply doing your best.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:39.343
It's a great book.

00:04:39.343 --> 00:04:41.200
His follow up book, "The Fifth Agreement"

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.130
built on those ideas as well.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.684
He advices us to be skeptical

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.600
but learn to listen.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.729
And that's more important in
this new year more than ever.

00:04:49.729 --> 00:04:51.630
I think we can all agree on that.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:54.470
Let's welcome New York
Times Best Selling Author,

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.249
Don Miguel Ruiz!

00:04:56.249 --> 00:04:57.563
What's up, man?

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.783
(audience applauds)

00:04:59.783 --> 00:05:01.363
How are you?

00:05:01.363 --> 00:05:02.373
- Wonderful, wonderful.

00:05:02.373 --> 00:05:05.690
It's a big pleasure to be on your show.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.940
- Oh my god, I just want
you to talk nonstop,

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.123
your accent is so cool, man.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.353
At the start of the hour,

00:05:12.353 --> 00:05:14.967
I read your quote from
"The Fifth Agreement",

00:05:14.967 --> 00:05:17.487
"Even the worst thing
that can happen to you

00:05:17.487 --> 00:05:20.379
"is meant to happen because
it's going to push you to grow."

00:05:20.379 --> 00:05:23.025
I think it's a quote, obviously,
all of us needed to hear

00:05:23.025 --> 00:05:24.985
desperately in 2020.

00:05:24.985 --> 00:05:27.835
But let's bring Kailyn
back into the conversation.

00:05:27.835 --> 00:05:30.456
Earlier she told us how her relationship

00:05:30.456 --> 00:05:32.892
with her brother was
shattered this summer.

00:05:32.892 --> 00:05:34.240
It was devastating.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:36.350
And as the mom of two
adopted Black daughters,

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.686
she couldn't stand what
he posted on social media

00:05:38.686 --> 00:05:40.612
about the Black Lives Matter Movement.

00:05:40.612 --> 00:05:43.880
When she confronted him,
everything fell apart.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.830
Which is, like I said, that's devastating

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.599
and very hard.

00:05:47.599 --> 00:05:49.440
There's hard conversations there.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.140
So Kailyn, you have a question
for Don Miguel, right?

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.750
- Yeah, I do.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.380
The quote that you just
talked about, Kelly,

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.985
also resinates with me

00:05:58.985 --> 00:06:01.870
because I do feel as if,

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:04.050
there's something that
I'm supposed to learn

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.663
from this experience and grow from,

00:06:06.663 --> 00:06:10.480
but I haven't quite
figured out what it is yet.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.410
And then the second thing is

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:16.920
if I am trying to
reconcile with my brother,

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:21.319
how can I remain an ally to my daughters

00:06:21.319 --> 00:06:24.870
and still reconcile with him?

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.977
- First you have to understand
that this is your story,

00:06:26.977 --> 00:06:30.673
and you are the main
character in that story.

00:06:31.514 --> 00:06:33.426
And you have priorities.

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:36.732
The first priority is always yourself.

00:06:36.732 --> 00:06:41.732
The second priority is the
ones that you love the most,

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:47.367
in your case, your little
girl is extremely important

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:52.200
and you have all the right to protect her

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:56.960
and to push away from her
whatever can harm her.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.625
In that case, with your brother,

00:06:59.625 --> 00:07:01.426
if he feels that way,

00:07:01.426 --> 00:07:06.426
well, your priority is your
daughter not your brother.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.460
It doesn't mean that you don't love him,

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:14.770
but will not allow him
to hurt your daughter,

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:16.422
you will protect her.

00:07:16.422 --> 00:07:21.422
Perhaps it's important to
separate for a little while,

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.160
let him, if he can, recapitulate

00:07:26.932 --> 00:07:29.039
and see that he was wrong,

00:07:29.039 --> 00:07:34.039
but you don't have to take
with you all that pain,

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:36.360
you don't need it, it's not yours.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:40.880
It's poison that comes from
somebody else, it's not yours.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:41.713
- I love that.

00:07:41.713 --> 00:07:44.300
- For you, the most important
is your own daughter

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:46.725
and first, yourself.

00:07:46.725 --> 00:07:50.560
That you will forgive your brother

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:55.392
even if he don't deserve to be forgiven,

00:07:55.392 --> 00:07:58.739
just because you love yourself

00:07:58.739 --> 00:08:03.739
and you don't want that
issue to keep hurting you.

00:08:03.861 --> 00:08:06.260
I don't know if I'm making any sense.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.130
- No, that was great.
- But it came from my heart.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.666
- No, I love that.

00:08:10.666 --> 00:08:13.140
And I think it's important to remember too

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:16.270
that forgiving doesn't mean agreeing.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:17.550
You know, you can forgive someone

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.887
and still not agree with them.

00:08:19.887 --> 00:08:23.660
But Kailyn, I felt like
that was pretty helpful,

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:24.950
did that make sense to you?

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.200
- Yeah, it does.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.046
I see now that the lesson
I need to learn in this

00:08:31.046 --> 00:08:36.046
is to forgive so that my story
is peaceful within myself,

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.870
because they're all living
their own stories too.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.596
So thank you for that advice.

00:08:42.596 --> 00:08:45.254
- I loved this, thank
you so much, Don Miguel.

00:08:45.254 --> 00:08:47.140
Check out "The Four Agreements"

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:49.840
and "The Fifth Agreement"
wherever you get your books.

